            {
                "entry_id": "ac17bc52-3323-3bed-b8fb-f501d85675dc",
                "word": "gibelin",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "9dc90772-83a5-4c2e-b8df-9ee8387e9634",
                        "entry_id": "ac17bc52-3323-3bed-b8fb-f501d85675dc",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "gibelins"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "33aeef0f-2ef4-3a72-8461-a8b2d0903747",
                        "entry_id": "ac17bc52-3323-3bed-b8fb-f501d85675dc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Membre de la faction qui soutenait les prétentions du Saint-Empire romain germanique, contre la papauté, sur l’Italie."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "930342f6-1ed5-442f-a956-d1a05900cea6",
                                "sense_id": "33aeef0f-2ef4-3a72-8461-a8b2d0903747",
                                "text": "C’était un fier gibelin que cet Auberti, plus gibelin que Dante lui-même ; car, ne pouvant supporter l’Italie où l’empire avait des ennemis, il vint à Genève, ville toute impériale, comme le dit si judicieusement M. le professeur ; bref, il s’établit ici, et c’est de lui que nous descendons."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e3019620-f8b5-3751-b8b7-f34f6aaa2c3d",
                        "entry_id": "ac17bc52-3323-3bed-b8fb-f501d85675dc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Les Guelfes et les Gibelins, les personnes les plus opposées."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0eb37f08-b9b8-48d5-a807-e37f2014dae6",
                                "sense_id": "e3019620-f8b5-3751-b8b7-f34f6aaa2c3d",
                                "text": "Mme de Maintenon, Mme de Thiange, Guelfes et Gibelins, songez que tout est rassemblé."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "10e87bb6-55cf-4d6a-b8f0-5706a4fb9e35",
                        "source_entry_id": "ac17bc52-3323-3bed-b8fb-f501d85675dc",
                        "target_lang_word": "Staufer",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Staufer",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6d495f06-d0cf-3073-ad63-cbc727c7b43a",
                                        "entry_id": "5b05eb41-6ea1-3e4d-87dd-f06527ed3e5c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Angehöriger des gleichnamigen Geschlechtes"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Adel"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "99ffc0ec-5398-4165-8f62-c811f34e5e33",
                                                "sense_id": "6d495f06-d0cf-3073-ad63-cbc727c7b43a",
                                                "text": "Friedrich Barbarossa war wohl der bekannteste Sprössling des Geschlechtes der Staufer."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d60a8689-a125-4dcb-9aa3-8d345253c654",
                                                "sense_id": "6d495f06-d0cf-3073-ad63-cbc727c7b43a",
                                                "text": "„Auch in der Literatur und in der bildenden Kunst war die Geschichte der Staufer ein immer wieder mit nationalem Pathos aufgegriffenes Thema.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "cdce0ab6-e6ef-4615-beb4-cad85b01f359",
                        "source_entry_id": "ac17bc52-3323-3bed-b8fb-f501d85675dc",
                        "target_lang_word": "Ghibelline",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Ghibelline",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3de53a15-a434-31a2-9826-463778468de3",
                                        "entry_id": "7b7c9b80-c334-36b3-9e87-353b2f2fa1f1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In the politics of medieval Italian city states, any member of a faction that supported the Holy Roman Emperor in a long struggle against the Guelphs and the Pope."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ac224d80-2a68-411a-bc91-4e0e6d16568d",
                                                "sense_id": "3de53a15-a434-31a2-9826-463778468de3",
                                                "text": "These two factions came to be called Guelphs and Ghibellines respectively. The Guelphs were the supporters of the Popes, the Ghibellines of the Emperors. The Guelphs upheld the temporal supremacy of the Pope: the Ghibellines would separate temporal from spiritual authority. The Guelphs resisted the establishment of complete imperial government in the cities of northern Italy: the Ghibellines, with the glories of the old Roman Empire before their eyes, longed to see Italy welded together into a single nation, and governed and controlled by the strong hands of the emperor."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3af93698-2d24-427a-9624-f50f1a438983",
                                                "sense_id": "3de53a15-a434-31a2-9826-463778468de3",
                                                "text": "2012, Elizabeth K. Haller, Dante Aleghieri (1265—1321), Lister M. Matheson (editor), Icons of the Middle Ages, Volume 1, ABC-Clio (Greenwood) page 246,\nThe Ghibellines gained power in Florence in 1249 and immediately banished the Guelphs. Ezzelino da Romano was one of the leaders of the Ghibelline movement and had a reputation for cruelty. He is depicted by Dante as a tyrant in The Divine Comedy."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "634d89be-f8d2-40f3-a5fe-0f9c10b04193",
                                                "sense_id": "3de53a15-a434-31a2-9826-463778468de3",
                                                "text": "More specifically, Fastello is said to address those Ghibellines who resided in the Valdarno area."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
